test_voronoi_gold -- del_vor against the lanl/voronoi test meshes (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_voronoi_gold_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]   12 runs, about 1 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  del_vor -avs MESH.inp -o MESH.stor                  FEHM .stor
  del_vor -avs MESH.inp -o MESH_c.stor -compress      compressed .stor
  del_vor -avs MESH.inp -type pflotran -o MESH.uge    PFLOTRAN .uge
  del_vor -avs MESH.inp -type tough2 -o MESH_MESH     TOUGH2 MESH

  on the three meshes of lanl/voronoi test/sanity_check (inputs/,
  copied unchanged, see inputs/NOTICE):

  mesh_2D     9 vertices, 8 triangles: a 2 x 2 square
  mesh_3D     116 vertices, 384 tets: a cube of side 1e6, graded
              toward one corner (vertex spacing 1.56e4 to 2.5e5)
  simple_3D   8 vertices, 5 tets: a unit cube

  The gold .stor files were written by LaGriT (matbld2d_stor,
  matbld3d_nstor), so matching them is also a first check against
  LaGriT. The gold .uge and MESH files were written by lanl/voronoi.

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_voronoi_gold.py; tolerance 1e-12, relative)

  stor        every volume and every vertex-pair coefficient against
              the gold .stor, plain and compressed
  layout      the .stor blocks fit together (row and diagonal
              pointers, sorted columns, symmetric matrix, NCON_MAX)
  balance     the control volumes add up to the mesh volume (area),
              computed here from the .inp
  uge         volumes and connection areas against the gold .uge, and
              against the .stor of the same run (A/d, volumes)
  MESH        TOUGH2 records field by field against gold (names,
              material, ISOT equal; numbers within one unit of the
              last printed digit), and volumes against the .stor

  MEASURED: values written by the compressed .stor; connections in
  the .uge; MESH lines byte-identical to gold.

KNOWN DIFFERENCES FROM THE GOLD FILES (by design, not failures)

  - .uge and MESH leave out zero-area connections (|A| <= 1e-12 of
    the largest). voronoi's 3D .uge did too; its 2D .uge listed 4.
    Zero-area connections stay in the .stor (LaGriT's layout).
  - 4 lines of the 3D MESH differ in the last printed digit: values
    exactly halfway (1.5625e16, 3.90625e9) that voronoi's round-off
    pushed up and del_vor rounds to even.
  - voronoi's own 3D .uge volumes differ from LaGriT's by 1.5e-13;
    del_vor's differ from LaGriT's by 1.5e-15 (circumcenters computed
    relative to a vertex, not from 4x4 determinants).

PICTURES (logs/)

  mesh_2D.svg     the triangles, the Voronoi dual (computed here), A/d
                  on every edge (green: equal to gold), area per vertex
  mesh_3D.svg     the tets' edges, vertices colored by control volume,
                  the 120 zero-area connections dashed
  simple_3D.svg   the same for the cube, with A/d on every edge

FILES

  run_voronoi_gold_tests.sh   runner (work/, logs/)
  check_voronoi_gold.py       checks, pictures, summary.html
  inputs/                     meshes and gold files from lanl/voronoi
